''Those much-anticipated drop rates for Perilous Moons and the Colosseum are here! Along with more Varlamore tweaks and a peek at next week's update.''

==Feedback & Upcoming Changes - 4th April==
We’re back regarding the most recent update and what our plans our for the next changes regarding content within the Colosseum. '''Before we jump in, we want to stress that these are the proposed changes, but we are open to hearing feedback from you all beforehand.'''

===Modifiers===
The team has seen plenty of feedback since first part of the Shining Kingdom released, but the focus in our most recent discussions revolves around Civitas Illa Fortis’ iconic landmark. We've been discussing just how we can modify those Modifiers to make the Colosseum feel better for everyone. Let’s look at what we’re going to change:

===Bees!===
* Given a longer delay before they respawn.
* Given a longer delay before they move to their next tile.
* Look to improve the visibility of Bees.

===Doom===
* There will now be three tiers of Doom. Each tier will allow you to take up to 15, 10 or 5 Stacks of Doom (respectively) before meeting your end.
* Doom will now reset back to 0 stacks at the end of each wave.
* We’re removing the Soul Reaper Axe & Divine Potions from adding to stacks of Doom.

===Myopia===
* Remove the ability to autocast spells without being affected.
** This means you’ll still be able to manually cast with this Modifier.

===Relentless===
* Change to how the additional accuracy is applied to monster hits.
** Stack 1 ignores 33% defence.
** Stack 2 ignores 66% defence.
** Stack 3 ignores all defences.
** Additional damage per stack is left unchanged.

===Totemic===
* Increase cooldown before respawning a new totem if the first is killed.
* The Amount of healing will be reduced.

===Doom Scorpion (REMOVED)===
* Even though they will be removed, we'll put them somewhere you can visit them in-game.

===Mantimayhem (NEW)===
* Manticores orb attacks become stronger, each time this is chosen.
** This makes missing your flicks slightly more punishing but wouldn't change how many times you need to flick.

===Drop Rates===
Another key piece of feedback we’ve seen is that the drop rates for the uniques you can obtain went against what was initially mentioned in previous newsposts.

Although things can change between an initial pitch, later newsposts and sometimes even before a release, it’s completely understandable that the information we present is what you will attach to. We’ll make it much clearer throughout development which areas are subject to change and highlight those that should not - we've already got some thoughts on how to do this!

As for what we can do, first we’re going to make it so that both the Sunfire Armour pieces and the Echo Crystals can be obtained from completing Wave 3 onwards. Not only that, but we're making it so you will hit the unique loot table more often, with a higher chance given to the Sunfire Armour pieces. As for the Tonalztics, they will only obtainable from completing Wave 7 onwards.

We’ll be updating the original image with Colosseum drop rates to show exactly how these proposed changes will impact things.
===Unique Improvements===
Not only have we improved the drop rate for the Colosseum’s uniques, we’ve also attempted to tackle the feeling that some of the items are underwhelming when compared to the content they come from. So, let’s look at the changes!

===Echo Crystals===
These boots will now be made for much more than walking, as when you convert the Guardian Boots to the Echo Boots this will now be a permanent change, regardless of if you have any charges or not. We’re also giving you the ability to turn off the Echo Boots effect, which means you can really pick and choose your moments to punish your enemies!

As for the Echo Crystal charges themselves, we’re upping the number of charges per Echo Crystal to 6,000 and increasing the maximum charges on the Boots to 60,000, that’s roughly 2.5x more use from the Crystals and 6x more space in those Boots. As a final note, we’ll be increasing the Alch price of Echo Crystals to reflect it's value more accurately.

===Tonalztics of Ralos===
We’re going to remove the 50% cap on Defence reduction from its Special Attack, giving you the freedom to use it as much as you possibly can. Just like the Echo Crystals, we're upping the Alch price of this item too!

===Sunfire Fanatic Armour===
While we're not changing anything about the Armour pieces, their Alch prices will be adjusted accordingly!

===Dizanna’s Quiver===
Last but certainly not least, let’s talk about the real reason you’re all taking on Sol Heredit. We’ve consistently seen the feedback from you all that the Quiver looks underwhelming, especially when it comes to its size and grandeur. We showed off these previous concepts before but want to see what you think one more time to make sure we’re heading in the right direction. Let us know what you think about the new versions!

