===Hunters' Rumours - Drop rates===
One area we forgot to include in yesterday's update when talking Varlamore were the drop rates for Hunters' Rumours. So not only are we going to give you the rates for the uniques but we're also going to give you the drop rates for Creature parts when doing a Rumour. Please remember these are just the drop rates and aren't guranteed after X creatures hunted.

* Guild Hunter Outfit pieces: '''1/50''' (any tier of Loot Sack)
* Huntsman's Kit: '''1/50''' (Adapt, Expert or Master Loot Sack)
* Quetzal Pet: '''1/1000''' (Expert or Master Loot Sack)
* Enhanced Whistle Blueprint: '''1/50''' (any tier of Loot Sack) - ''Pity Drop at 100 Rumours''
* Perfected Whistle Blueprint: '''1/50''' (Expert or Master Loot Sack) - ''Pity Drop at 250 Rumours (Requires the Enhanced Whistle)''

Creature Part Drops

* Box traps: '''1/50'''
* Pitfall traps: '''1/15'''
* Butterflies: '''1/75'''
* Birds: '''1/20'''
* Deadfall traps: '''1/15'''
* Tracking: '''1/15'''
* Falcon: '''1/10'''
* Herbiboar: '''1/7'''
* Lizards: '''1/25'''

We really appreciate everyone’s time, feedback and patience with us on this exciting new content!

==Changelog - April 3rd==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
===Varlamore Updates===
'''Colosseum'''

* The Ranged Warbanders have been given a little buff, so their ranged level more accurately reflects the rest of their stats. Watch out though, as this means they will hit a little harder now!
* We've reduced the Warband Melee's maxhit to give you a little more of a fighting chance up against those fellas.
* Those taking on the Colosseum will now receive the correct number of Glory for stacked modifiers.
* We've upped the Colosseum security so you'll no longer find NPCs wandering the arena if they aren't supposed to be there.
* All of the Fortis Colosseum NPCs now have their full and correct attack style information when using Monster Examine.
* You can now trade the Dizana's Quiver for a total of 4,000 Sunfire Splinters by talking to Minimus.
* We have slightly reduced the number of Sunfire Splinters obtainable in Wave 1, and increased the number gathered from waves 9-12. So while you'll receive 20% less Splinters on your first wave, if you make it through those later rounds, you'll see a lot more!

'''Perilous Moons'''

* We've taken a look at the Eclipse Boss and how much damage she's taking when at low hp, so you should no longer hit so many 1s!
* Sulphur Nagua's special attack will no longer bump them out of combat (which removes the window of opportunity for other pesky enemies getting a turn in when they shouldn't!)
* When fighting Moon bosses, the Ring of Recoil now correctly loses charges.
* Sipping tea from camps in the ruins will no longer be delayed during Perilous Moons.
* We've removed the forced camera movement when traversing Perilous Moons to make the journey more comfortable.
* To make it easier to escape the Perilous Moons bosses, we've made quick-escape the default option for the stairs.
* To reflect the lore around the Perilous Moons dungeon being newly discovered, you'll no longer find the diary entries detailing the dungeon's potions during the quest, only when you revisit the area.
* It's now consistently possible to kill Eclipse Moon during the Clone phase - even with single hitting weapons!
* We've now made it easier to tell when you've succeeded with the Fishing minigame during the Neypotzli dungeon, so now, when you have your net in the right place, you're guaranteed 1 fish, when you have it in the right place and succeed the roll, you'll receive 2 fish plus XP.
* You can now use a Stab attack style with the Dual Macuahuitl.

'''General'''

* You can now cover all of your Falconry fun with a one-time fee, and it's easier than ever - we've added the ability to right-click pay option on Matthias!
* Master hunters can relax, we've fixed a bug preventing you from using the Hunter Guild teleport on your Skill and Max Capes when you had used all of your Chinchompa teleports.
* The Huntsman's Kit will now correctly let you store all your hunter items - however, black chinchompas will wriggle free and won't be stored in your kit.
* We've tweaked the way the Hunters' Rumours work so you'll go a little less dry on the drops for many of the rumour creatures.
* A bug has been fixed which means you will now only be able to use the Meat Sack for Hunter activities.
* We've upped Irit Tar ranged strength to +60, so you'll get a little more bang for your muck! (see what we did there?)
* The Moonlight Potion now has the correct description, factoring in its boost to attack and strength alongside defense.
* For those undertaking A Ribbiting Tale, you can no longer escape a certain villainous frog's wrath by walking away. The furious frog will now continue to be aggro when you come back in range.
* Wyrms are back on the menu, boys! We've made sure Wyrms are showing in the Slayer Log.
* The stump in the Oasis no longer stops you taking an axe if you are carrying a combat axe.
* The Civitas illa Fortis teleport in the Portal Nexus interface now has the correct icon.
* The quetzals in Fortis have had a reshuffle, so you'll now find the more commonly used bird closer to a teleport.
* We've increased the maximum capacity of the Portal Nexus, so it can contain all teleports once again.
* An issue has been fixed where Echo Boots were losing charges in PvP scenarios.
* The Mixed Hide costume set can now be stored in the POH Costume room.
* Group Ironmen will now be able to correctly share hunter mixes and butterflies with their group.
* We've reduced a clue scroll requirement to mean you only need one piece of the Sunfire armour set to complete it.
* Your Sunfire Runes will give you even more XP as we have doubled those rates!
* Sapphire Glacialis butterflies now correctly boost defence when they are released.

===Other Changes===
* We've fixed a bug which occurred following the addition of Varlamore that caused the Fang to roll incorrect accuracy during ToA.
* If a player is prevented from chopping the mahogany and teak trees in Murcaily's Hardwood Grove due to having not helped out around the village enough, Murcaily will now warn them of this before trying to take 100 sticks from them for entry.
* The dark chests of the Isle of Souls no longer claim that you might have received a Medium Clue Scroll every time you loot them.
* Equipping the Lightbearer shortly before your special attack energy was due to restore will no longer delay the energy restoration.
* The werewolf who receives the stick in the underground Agility course no longer wanders around so much.
* If you need to get replacement railings from Lawgof during the Dwarf Cannon quest, he now gives as many replacements as you still need, rather than just one.

===PvP Rota===

