==Perilous Moons & Colosseum Drop Rates==
===Perilous Moons===
With every boss encounter comes the burning question: 'What are the drop rates for the rewards?' Well, the wait is over. We’re revealing the much-anticipated drop rates for the Perilous Moons bosses! Here’s what you need to know:

'''Defeating a Moons of Peril boss grants you a 1/56 chance to secure a random item from their exclusive drop table.'''

Blood Moon of Peril - 1/56 chance after defeating the Blood Moon boss to obtain a piece of Blood Moon gear:

* Blood Moon Armour Pieces
* Dual Macuahuitl

Blue Moon of Peril - 1/56 chance after defeating the Blue Moon boss to obtain a piece of Blue Moon gear:

* Blue Moon Armour Pieces
* Blue Moon Spear

Eclipse Moon of Peril - 1/56 chance after defeating the Eclipse Moon boss to obtain a piece of Eclipse Moon gear:

* Eclipse Moon Armour Pieces
* Eclipse Atlatl

'''Furthermore, upon defeating all three bosses in one run, you'll be given ''an additional 1/56'' chance at ''any'' item!''' This boosts your overall odds significantly to 1/14, making these rewards more common than the average Barrows item.

In a move to enhance your looting experience, we've also implemented a duplication protection system. This means you won't receive duplicate items from a set until you've completed the set, ensuring a smoother progression towards collecting all set pieces.

On that note, let’s continue with Fortis Colosseum drop rates…

===Fortis Colosseum===
[[File:Varlamore Tweaks & Drop Rates (1).png|600px|center]]

Once you've completed Wave 6 and for each wave afterwards, the Unique Drop Table is unlocked. If you roll on this table you do not roll on the Normal Drop Table for that wave. Glory will NEVER affect your odds. The base for rolling on the Unique Drop Table is 1/220. This number can be modified based on your current wave +1, which equals to:
* Wave 6 - 1/108
* Wave 7 - 1/92
* Wave 8 - 1/76
* Wave 9 - 1/60
* Wave 10 - 1/44
* Wave 11 - 1/28

If you're lucky enough to roll up the Unique Drop Table, a second roll will determine which unique item you receive. Otherwise, you'll be rolling against that wave's normal drop table. Here are the odds for the Unique Drop Table:
* Echo Crystal - 6/10*
* Sunfire Fanatic Armour Piece - 3/10**
* Tonalztics of Ralos - 1/10

Other Rare Items include:
* Smol Heredit - 1/200***
* Dizana's Quiver - Only acquired upon a completion of the Colosseum.****

<nowiki>* Rolling an Echo Crystal will also have a 1/10 chance of receiving either 2 or 3 Echo Crystals instead.</nowiki>

<nowiki>** Obtaining these will favour pieces you haven't already received, otherwise it is random.</nowiki>

<nowiki>*** The pet can only be rolled on completion of Wave 11 and its odds are not affected by any other factors.</nowiki>

<nowiki>**** You can also gamble Quivers for a 1/200 chance to receive Smol Heredit by talking to Minimus.</nowiki>

