==Next Week - Undead Pirates==
We've not got much to say here, but wanted to give you all a heads-up that our low-level Wilderness hotspot is releasing as part of next week's game update.

So if you're looking to dust off your Pure, now's the time to book some time off or plan an awfully suspicious, nondescript headache... For a full list of what to expect, here's everything we're looking to include in next week's update:

* Undead Pirates added and landscape changes to the Chaos Temple.
* New rewards in the form of Adamant seeds and the Teleport Anchoring Scroll (formerly named 'Blip blocking scroll', but now it has a nautical word in the mix!).
* A pirate ship on the Wilderness' eastern shore, housing a chest that players can open for additional loot rolls using keys that are dropped by Undead Pirates.
* An adjusted Hard Clue Scroll location, moving from the Chaos Temple itself to a spot just north, by the nearby Wilderness Obelisk.
* Improved opt-in loot and XP rates from the Wilderness Agility Course.
* Various QoL changes to imbued God cape purchasing and Wilderness Slayer, including improved Superior rates, NPC quantities ''and ''loot tables.
* Removing the PJ Timer on Worlds 318 and 319, with improved messaging to boot. The PJ Timer was never supposed to be added to these worlds and in-game messaging had been incorrect for some time, this change is to make good on what we said our plan was when first introducing the PJ Timer [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/pj-timer--new-broadcast-settings-?oldschool=1 in this blog from 2022] so that players who primarily enjoy a slightly different style of PKing might get the chance to jump back in!

If you're looking for a reminder on exactly what to expect, you can check out the original blog [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/low-level-wilderness-hotspot-deadman-2024--more?oldschool=1 here ] or get more information about some of the rewards and other content changes (listed above) [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/updated-undead-pirates-rewards--more---poll-blog?oldschool=1 in this poll blog.]

We'll see you in the Wilderness! Just remember to not bring anything you're not willing to lose, and to go easy on us if you see us out there…

